      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watertown%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in Watertown in 1826 and stayed open until 1993, serving the community for 167 years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watertown%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1986, Watertown was listed on the National Register of Historic Places as the Watertown Historic District, covering 60 acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watertown%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic district includes 75 buildings, most built after the Civil War and before World War I, with many white weatherboard structures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
